WEBVTT

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:02.160
Hey, have you heard?

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:06.900
In order to avoid people,
Aoyama basically never takes the train.

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:09.710
Really? That sounds like Aoyama.

00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:13.450
He'll have a rough time making it to
our game against Takada Academy tomorrow.

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:17.910
What's up?

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:20.370
Isn't that Aoyama?

00:00:21.070 --> 00:00:22.250
You're right.

00:00:28.990 --> 00:00:31.750
I may be able to give Aoyama 
a reason not to show up.

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:07.940
<b>#03</b>

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:07.940
<b>The Reason Aoyama-kun Isn't Here</b>

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:07.940
Mr. Zaizen! Thank you for treating us!

00:02:08.570 --> 00:02:10.400
I never said it was my treat.

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:15.270
It's our tradition to eat at a family
restaurant the day before a match!

00:02:15.270 --> 00:02:18.860
Stop making up traditions. 
I only treated you one time.

00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:21.090
You can't go into battle on an empty stomach!

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:25.580
We want to win tomorrow, right?
Right, Aoyama?

00:02:28.030 --> 00:02:30.040
I'm going home.

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:32.200
Why? He's treating us!

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:33.600
I just told you I didn't say that.

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:36.010
Look! It's the next head of 
the Zaizen family over here!

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:40.350
Aoyama, let's do some killer mixing
at the drink bar and start a revolution!

00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:43.260
I'd rather get home quickly
and take a shower.

00:02:46.050 --> 00:02:48.560
Looks like nature's providing you
with one right now.

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:53.570
Welcome.

00:02:53.570 --> 00:02:55.690
Can I take your order?

00:02:56.140 --> 00:02:57.700
This is some guerrilla downpour...

00:02:57.700 --> 00:02:59.850
We'll all start with the drink bar.

00:02:59.850 --> 00:03:01.560
It's right over there.

00:03:16.110 --> 00:03:17.840
So that's out, too?

00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:26.210
That looks gross. What's with that color?

00:03:26.210 --> 00:03:29.990
It's cola plus melon soda. 
It might look bad, but it's the best!

00:03:29.990 --> 00:03:32.140
I dipped a teabag in there as well.

00:03:32.470 --> 00:03:36.030
Well, let's prepare ourselves for making it
through the preliminaries tomorrow—

00:03:36.030 --> 00:03:37.110
Unacceptable.

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:43.700
It's beyond belief that Aoyama's 
playing for such a worthless team.

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:48.160
It's like giving a national 
cultural treasure to toddlers.

00:03:48.630 --> 00:03:52.440
You're that perverted forward from 
Oshigami-Minami, Takechi Akira!

00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:55.470
Ah, it's the worthless soccer team
from Fujimi High School.

00:03:55.470 --> 00:03:57.880
Who are you calling a worthless team?!

00:03:58.360 --> 00:03:59.690
Aoyama!

00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:04.230
Fancy running into you here.
What a coincidence.

00:04:04.230 --> 00:04:06.370
Stop it with the ab flexing!

00:04:06.370 --> 00:04:09.310
People call you a pervert because
you do that no matter where you are!

00:04:10.010 --> 00:04:14.270
And coincidence? Puh-lease. You always
come and watch our practice sessions.

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:19.870
Why would I lower myself to
watching a bunch of amateurs train?

00:04:19.870 --> 00:04:23.130
You may think those sunglasses in
your pocket are an adequate disguise,

00:04:23.130 --> 00:04:24.740
but they're conspicuous as hell!

00:04:25.540 --> 00:04:27.090
Well, if the cat's out of the bag—

00:04:27.090 --> 00:04:28.620
You're not even trying to keep it there!

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:32.790
So you're up against 
Takada Academy tomorrow?

00:04:32.790 --> 00:04:37.000
If we fielded our starting eleven
against them, we'd win at least five-nil.

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:40.040
And if we had Aoyama,

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:43.760
even the lowest estimate
would see us scoring ten goals.

00:04:46.030 --> 00:04:47.880
So what?

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:50.150
Hypothetical scenarios are so pointless.

00:04:50.150 --> 00:04:51.720
Let's eat.

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:55.340
No matter what you say, 
Aoyama's on our team.

00:04:55.340 --> 00:04:56.440
Go home, go home.

00:04:56.440 --> 00:05:00.900
This is why you're all worthless! 
You're not getting my point!

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:04.020
I'm saying you aren't fit
to be Aoyama's teammates!

00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:06.450
Shut up! There are other customers in here!

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:07.070
Stop shouting!

00:05:07.070 --> 00:05:08.880
What's going on?

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:10.290
A fight? That's so lame.

00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:12.390
Takechi-san, please calm down!

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:15.290
I can take your order now.

00:05:19.750 --> 00:05:21.460
It's finally here!

00:05:21.930 --> 00:05:24.420
Thank you for the food!

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:27.380
Hey, Aoyama, you're not going to eat?

00:05:28.860 --> 00:05:31.850
This jumbo Hamburg steak is addictive!
You should order it.

00:05:32.940 --> 00:05:34.810
Here's your jumbo Hamburg steak.

00:05:38.330 --> 00:05:41.980
You guys know nothing about Aoyama.

00:05:42.370 --> 00:05:43.310
What?

00:05:43.310 --> 00:05:45.940
Aoyama never eats out.

00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:51.100
He only eats nutritionally balanced 
meals he's prepared himself.

00:05:51.100 --> 00:05:54.870
He does that so he can stay in 
perfect shape as an athlete.

00:05:54.870 --> 00:05:57.140
He's not like you slobs,

00:05:57.140 --> 00:06:01.340
who pay no regard to your prelim match 
tomorrow and eat with reckless abandon.

00:06:06.210 --> 00:06:10.260
I think his germaphobia just prevents him
from eating food someone else has made.

00:06:10.790 --> 00:06:16.080
So, Aoyama, I will take care 
of this thing for you.

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:17.230
Now wait just one minute...

00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:21.310
That's actually my job.

00:06:21.310 --> 00:06:24.430
You already have the same dish
in front of you!

00:06:24.430 --> 00:06:27.280
This? It'll be gone in three seconds flat!

00:06:30.430 --> 00:06:32.700
Now, gimme that Hamb—

00:06:33.490 --> 00:06:35.660
You already finished it?!

00:06:38.620 --> 00:06:41.460
That pervert keeps provoking us!

00:06:45.330 --> 00:06:47.210
Your cheese-filled Hamburg steak.

00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:49.790
Huh? I didn't order that.

00:06:50.420 --> 00:06:52.180
The gentlemen over there 
ordered it for you.

00:06:52.750 --> 00:06:54.810
Yeah, yeah, yeah!

00:06:56.260 --> 00:06:59.600
I don't think you can beat me for speed.

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:03.560
You schmuck. You dare to challenge me?

00:07:03.560 --> 00:07:05.320
All right, then!

00:07:06.990 --> 00:07:08.730
It's a dead heat!

00:07:08.730 --> 00:07:11.640
The next battle is over the Japanese-style 
radish-topped Hamburg steak!

00:07:11.640 --> 00:07:13.450
Huh? Another Hamburg steak?

00:07:13.820 --> 00:07:16.230
How long is this rainstorm going to last?

00:07:17.410 --> 00:07:19.710
And how long will this 
speed-eating contest go on for?

00:07:19.710 --> 00:07:22.370
I guess at this point,
they're competing over who can eat more.

00:07:22.370 --> 00:07:26.330
Wow, only five more dishes and they 
will have conquered the whole menu!

00:07:26.330 --> 00:07:29.090
In that case,
the one who eats it all first wins.

00:07:29.620 --> 00:07:32.670
Takechi-san, let's call it quits! 
This is such a silly fight.

00:07:32.670 --> 00:07:35.970
Tachibana, there are fights 
you can't afford to lose.

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:37.810
<b>There are fights you
 can't afford to lose</b>

00:07:37.810 --> 00:07:44.190
Even if it wasn't our regular eleven, 
we lost the training match against them.

00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:45.690
<b>We lost</b>

00:07:45.690 --> 00:07:48.680
Losing against the same opponent twice?

00:07:48.680 --> 00:07:51.930
My pride won't allow it!

00:07:50.940 --> 00:07:53.070
<b>My pride won't allow it</b>

00:07:51.930 --> 00:07:54.780
No, wait. This has nothing to do with soccer!

00:07:53.130 --> 00:07:54.780
<b>This has nothing to do with soccer</b>

00:07:58.740 --> 00:08:02.040
They're finally on the last dish! 
It's everyone's favorite: curry and rice!

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:04.710
And now both contestants' hands
have stopped in midair!

00:08:05.800 --> 00:08:09.750
<i>To be honest, my stomach went 
way past capacity a long time ago.</i>

00:08:09.750 --> 00:08:12.250
<i>I feel like it can't even 
take another grain of rice.</i>

00:08:12.250 --> 00:08:12.930
<i>But you know what?</i>

00:08:14.090 --> 00:08:16.100
<i>Watch me, Aoyama!</i>

00:08:16.890 --> 00:08:20.850
<i>I am better than these scrubs
in every regard!</i>

00:08:21.330 --> 00:08:24.060
Takechi's powering through 
to the home stretch!

00:08:27.770 --> 00:08:34.150
<i>You and I... We met in middle school, 
at the training match for the Tokyo try-outs.</i>

00:08:35.450 --> 00:08:38.740
<i>I still remember the pass you made to me
in the youth internationals.</i>

00:08:39.240 --> 00:08:43.630
<i>It was the kind of pass
that guides you to the goal.</i>

00:08:43.630 --> 00:08:46.210
<i>I can't forget how it felt.</i>

00:08:51.460 --> 00:08:55.220
<i>No matter who they are, any forward
who receives a pass like that</i>

00:08:55.220 --> 00:08:57.820
<i>will want to receive it again.</i>

00:09:00.770 --> 00:09:04.600
<i>That's why I've tried everything 
I can to persuade him.</i>

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:07.020
<i>I wanted to conquer all of Japan with you.</i>

00:09:07.530 --> 00:09:09.160
The last bite!

00:09:09.160 --> 00:09:11.730
<i>Pass the ball to me like that once more!</i>

00:09:12.420 --> 00:09:14.280
Aoyama!

00:09:15.980 --> 00:09:18.700
"Seasonal dish: the mega-sized
 strawberry parfait?"

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:22.660
Takechi-san, this is the last item.

00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:25.620
You perfectionist.

00:09:25.620 --> 00:09:29.590
This... is our mega-sized 
strawberry parfait.

00:09:31.070 --> 00:09:35.010
Aoyama, that was one hell of a killer pass.

00:09:35.010 --> 00:09:36.550
Takechi-san!

00:09:37.370 --> 00:09:41.510
Hang in there, Takechi! I've brought 
my special hyper-mixed drink for you!

00:09:42.120 --> 00:09:43.990
Dessert goes into a different stomach.

00:09:44.870 --> 00:09:46.980
Looks like we win again.

00:09:49.110 --> 00:09:53.440
The rain's stopped, so I'm going home.

00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:57.700
So this place we went to last time 
with Kana was <i>so</i> delicious.

00:09:57.700 --> 00:09:59.410
Let's go there together.

00:09:59.410 --> 00:10:00.840
Yeah, I want to go!

00:10:00.840 --> 00:10:01.690
Kana?

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:05.330
<b>Tokyo Subdivision 
Preliminaries Arena</b>

00:10:05.750 --> 00:10:09.070
That damn clean freak! 
Where's that oddball got to?

00:10:09.070 --> 00:10:10.500
Where did he go?!

00:10:10.880 --> 00:10:14.270
Calm down, Zaizen.
He was here just a moment ago.

00:10:14.270 --> 00:10:15.510
He'll be back.

00:10:15.510 --> 00:10:17.960
Yeah, cool your jets.

00:10:18.550 --> 00:10:20.630
You guys are way too relaxed about this!

00:10:20.630 --> 00:10:23.740
The important first match of
the Inter-High preliminaries is today!

00:10:23.740 --> 00:10:26.230
Dammit, don't you know this already, Aoyama?!

00:10:31.110 --> 00:10:32.140
All right.

00:10:35.590 --> 00:10:37.530
What a drag.

00:10:37.530 --> 00:10:40.930
Why on earth must they insist on 
playing matches at our school?

00:10:40.930 --> 00:10:42.490
It just creates more work.

00:10:48.950 --> 00:10:50.620
Hey, you!

00:10:50.620 --> 00:10:53.590
Why are you washing the bottle I just washed?

00:10:54.240 --> 00:10:55.270
Well...

00:10:55.270 --> 00:10:56.550
"Well"?

00:10:57.570 --> 00:10:59.510
Because it's dirty.

00:11:02.220 --> 00:11:05.660
Then why don't you come and help me?

00:11:06.430 --> 00:11:09.390
All right! Are you done warming up?

00:11:09.390 --> 00:11:10.610
Yessir!

00:11:10.610 --> 00:11:13.940
But, Orihara-san,
this Fujimi High we're up against

00:11:13.940 --> 00:11:15.990
has that Aoyama dude playing for them.

00:11:15.990 --> 00:11:18.320
So what?

00:11:22.300 --> 00:11:26.470
It's not like I do this because I want to.

00:11:26.470 --> 00:11:29.310
My boyfriend happens to be
the captain of the team, so...

00:11:29.310 --> 00:11:31.500
Gross! What have they been doing in here?

00:11:32.450 --> 00:11:35.460
Oh, please put that box
on the shelf at the back.

00:11:35.890 --> 00:11:40.350
My boyfriend's a punk,
but he actually cares about soccer.

00:11:40.350 --> 00:11:43.820
He told me that today's opponent 
in the prelims are a real threat.

00:11:45.550 --> 00:11:47.350
His name...

00:11:48.070 --> 00:11:50.310
Why have you locked the door?

00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:53.150
Aoyama from Fujimi High School.

00:11:54.810 --> 00:11:57.230
You won't be getting out of here.

00:11:57.230 --> 00:11:59.590
Not until the match is over, anyway.

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:04.990
<b>Always showing
 off his six-pack!</b>

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:04.990
<b>Takechi Akira</b>

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:04.990
<b>Tachibana</b>

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:04.990
<b>New formula</b>

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:04.990
<b>The cleaning 
power will 
astonish you</b>

00:12:04.990 --> 00:12:07.990
<b>Bring on</b>

00:12:04.990 --> 00:12:07.990
the foul play

00:12:04.990 --> 00:12:07.990
<b>Orihara Youji</b>

00:12:04.990 --> 00:12:07.990
<b>Kana</b>

00:12:07.990 --> 00:12:09.950
<b>Tokyo Subdivision 
Preliminaries Arena</b>

00:12:10.360 --> 00:12:13.920
This is a surprisingly big crowd 
for a subdivision preliminary.

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:17.040
It's because Fujimi High School
has that Aoyama kid.

00:12:17.040 --> 00:12:19.240
They're probably all here for him.

00:12:19.240 --> 00:12:21.860
I see. He's just that popular, huh?

00:12:22.710 --> 00:12:26.650
This is weird, though.
I don't see him anywhere.

00:12:29.030 --> 00:12:30.810
Aoyama isn't coming.

00:12:30.810 --> 00:12:33.100
I'm seriously going to murder him!

00:12:33.100 --> 00:12:35.170
The match is starting.

00:12:35.170 --> 00:12:37.870
Let's keep this huddle going 
just a little bit longer.

00:12:39.070 --> 00:12:41.380
I can't find Aoyama-kun anywhere!

00:12:41.380 --> 00:12:44.760
Seriously?! What's that 
chronically late fool playing at?

00:12:44.760 --> 00:12:47.170
I-I'll go look again!

00:12:47.170 --> 00:12:49.640
<i>Aoyama going AWOL is an issue,</i>

00:12:49.640 --> 00:12:52.040
<i>but we also got a bad draw
with this first opponent.</i>

00:12:53.220 --> 00:12:57.090
<i>It's not like Takada Academy 
has any standout players,</i>

00:12:57.090 --> 00:13:00.410
<i>but everyone on the team
is physically solid and runs a lot.</i>

00:13:01.560 --> 00:13:05.430
<i>And they don't shy away from
a bit of foul play in order to win.</i>

00:13:06.520 --> 00:13:09.390
<i>They're famous for being a team 
that likes to rough other teams up.</i>

00:13:13.220 --> 00:13:14.810
Son of a...

00:13:14.810 --> 00:13:16.770
<b>Soccer Team</b>

00:13:16.770 --> 00:13:20.230
<b>Conquer the Nation
Takada Academy Soccer Team</b>

00:13:17.880 --> 00:13:20.230
I can't let you play in that match.

00:13:24.210 --> 00:13:25.150
Don't move!

00:13:27.390 --> 00:13:29.120
I'll scream otherwise.

00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:32.320
I see.

00:13:33.120 --> 00:13:34.900
You play dirty.

00:13:36.110 --> 00:13:37.420
Huh? Wha—

00:13:39.480 --> 00:13:40.380
What happened?

00:13:41.380 --> 00:13:44.270
When I thought about the fact that 
I'm locked in here, I suddenly...

00:13:44.270 --> 00:13:47.800
So not only are you a clean freak, 
but you're also claustrophobic?!

00:13:47.800 --> 00:13:49.590
Don't touch me.

00:13:49.590 --> 00:13:51.260
You're such a pain!

00:13:51.940 --> 00:13:56.000
Just being locked in made you
break out in a cold sweat and collapse...

00:13:56.000 --> 00:13:58.230
And you're a severe germaphobe, aren't you?

00:13:59.160 --> 00:14:03.470
Can you even play soccer, a game 
where you keep running into people?

00:14:04.910 --> 00:14:07.160
It's impossible to play this sport 
without getting dirty.

00:14:09.100 --> 00:14:10.950
They blasted it in on the counter.

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:12.830
Takada Academy bag themselves another goal.

00:14:13.290 --> 00:14:15.790
All right! Goal number two!

00:14:15.790 --> 00:14:17.140
Damn.

00:14:17.140 --> 00:14:20.490
Once they scored, they shored up
their defense and waited to counterattack.

00:14:20.490 --> 00:14:24.250
Even though they look like delinquents, 
they take soccer seriously.

00:14:25.940 --> 00:14:30.180
<i>Where are you at a time like this, Aoyama?</i>

00:14:31.180 --> 00:14:33.140
Just another thirty minutes.

00:14:33.830 --> 00:14:37.100
Does your boyfriend know about this?

00:14:39.800 --> 00:14:41.060
Of course he doesn't.

00:14:41.060 --> 00:14:43.120
You looked so shifty just then.

00:14:43.120 --> 00:14:44.970
N-N-No, I didn't!

00:14:44.970 --> 00:14:47.030
I'm doing this on my own!

00:14:48.100 --> 00:14:48.990
Stop...

00:14:51.970 --> 00:14:53.380
Gotou Moka.

00:14:54.910 --> 00:14:58.870
Anyone who makes Aoyama-kun suffer
has to answer to me.

00:14:59.800 --> 00:15:02.050
How did you... The lock!

00:15:02.050 --> 00:15:05.800
This kind of cheap lock
won't even stop me for ten seconds.

00:15:06.710 --> 00:15:10.680
Some people saw a girl and Aoyama-kun
walking in the direction of the clubhouses,

00:15:10.680 --> 00:15:12.680
so I unlocked them one by one to check.

00:15:14.520 --> 00:15:16.640
Aoyama-kun, please hurry! 
The match has started!

00:15:24.520 --> 00:15:27.780
Fifteen minutes remain,
and Aoyama is missing.

00:15:27.780 --> 00:15:28.840
Might be time to pack up.

00:15:28.840 --> 00:15:30.140
You said it.

00:15:32.910 --> 00:15:34.470
That idiot.

00:15:34.470 --> 00:15:37.150
Aoyama-kun!

00:15:35.310 --> 00:15:37.370
Aoyama has finally made it on to the field!

00:15:37.150 --> 00:15:40.730
Aoyama-kun!

00:15:37.370 --> 00:15:41.410
Fifteen minutes left, two goals behind. 
That's an uphill task, even for Aoyama.

00:15:42.360 --> 00:15:44.230
What were you doing?

00:15:44.230 --> 00:15:45.870
And why do you have a brush?

00:15:45.870 --> 00:15:46.880
Zaizen-san.

00:15:47.980 --> 00:15:49.840
I'm going to pass to you.

00:15:53.110 --> 00:15:55.010
<i>Why is he here?</i>

00:15:55.880 --> 00:15:59.350
Ha. So you've finally 
shown your face, Aoyama.

00:15:59.350 --> 00:16:01.980
I've been waiting to take you on.

00:16:01.980 --> 00:16:05.690
But it's really unfortunate that 
there are only fifteen minutes left.

00:16:01.980 --> 00:16:05.690
<b>Takada</b>

00:16:01.980 --> 00:16:05.690
<b>1st</b>

00:16:01.980 --> 00:16:05.690
<b>2nd</b>

00:16:01.980 --> 00:16:05.690
<b>ET</b>

00:16:01.980 --> 00:16:05.690
<b>Fujimi</b>

00:16:12.570 --> 00:16:13.800
Aoyama!

00:16:14.780 --> 00:16:16.740
Aoyama's first touch!

00:16:16.740 --> 00:16:18.700
What will he do now?

00:16:24.620 --> 00:16:26.580
That's way too far for a pass!

00:16:26.900 --> 00:16:29.990
Ishida, get back! He's going for goal!

00:16:31.850 --> 00:16:33.470
Saved by the bar!

00:16:33.940 --> 00:16:38.180
He's really up for this, going for
a long-range shot after just one touch!

00:16:39.070 --> 00:16:42.160
He's only made one play,
but I can already smell a goal coming!

00:16:42.160 --> 00:16:45.100
So cool!

00:16:45.100 --> 00:16:47.560
That's Aoyama. Shoot! Shoot!

00:16:48.060 --> 00:16:50.530
Tch. "I'm going to pass to you," my ass.

00:16:50.530 --> 00:16:53.280
See! That's our Aoyama right there!

00:16:53.280 --> 00:16:54.270
Did you see that?

00:16:54.270 --> 00:16:55.240
Right on!

00:16:55.240 --> 00:16:58.530
I told you not to give him 
space or time on the ball!

00:16:58.530 --> 00:16:59.660
It's dangerous!

00:16:59.660 --> 00:17:00.700
Yessir! I'm sorry!

00:17:00.700 --> 00:17:04.180
<i>Damn, so </i>this <i>is Aoyama...</i>

00:17:04.180 --> 00:17:09.110
<i>How can he move so fast, yet keep
the ball at his feet like it's on a string?</i>

00:17:09.110 --> 00:17:11.590
He scores! Goal number one for Aoyama!

00:17:12.210 --> 00:17:15.340
<i>Dammit! He's in a totally different league.</i>

00:17:15.340 --> 00:17:21.810
<i>But you know, soccer's not 
a clean game. You get me?</i>

00:17:24.440 --> 00:17:26.230
Do it!

00:17:28.630 --> 00:17:32.150
Put more people on him! 
Don't let him get away!

00:17:32.460 --> 00:17:35.370
It's amazing that he can be surrounded
and still keep the ball.

00:17:35.370 --> 00:17:36.370
Hey, now...

00:17:36.370 --> 00:17:39.480
They're being way too obvious 
about wanting to hurt Aoyama.

00:17:43.070 --> 00:17:45.370
He crossed while being surrounded.

00:17:45.370 --> 00:17:47.170
And it's on a dime!

00:17:47.910 --> 00:17:49.630
How did he even <i>see </i>that?

00:17:51.480 --> 00:17:53.380
Aoyama got sent flying!

00:17:57.010 --> 00:17:59.970
Goal! It's two apiece! We're tied!

00:18:01.160 --> 00:18:02.430
Aoyama!

00:18:08.760 --> 00:18:10.740
Yeah, that warranted a card.

00:18:10.740 --> 00:18:12.530
What, really?

00:18:12.530 --> 00:18:15.640
Bastard! What the hell?!

00:18:14.170 --> 00:18:15.640
Zaizen!

00:18:15.640 --> 00:18:17.590
That was totally on purpose!

00:18:17.590 --> 00:18:19.240
Cut the crap!

00:18:19.780 --> 00:18:22.700
I just had too much momentum.

00:18:24.570 --> 00:18:26.930
Hey, are you okay?

00:18:26.930 --> 00:18:28.380
I'm fine.

00:18:28.380 --> 00:18:29.920
You're...

00:18:30.510 --> 00:18:32.030
totally not fine!

00:18:32.030 --> 00:18:33.080
What do you mean?

00:18:33.080 --> 00:18:34.380
Stop pretending!

00:18:34.860 --> 00:18:37.340
Aoyama's movements have 
suddenly become stilted!

00:18:39.300 --> 00:18:42.830
Once his uncleanliness 
crosses a certain threshold,

00:18:42.830 --> 00:18:45.650
Aoyama-kun gets so stressed out 
that he can't play properly.

00:18:45.650 --> 00:18:47.480
Let's put that away, shall we?

00:18:47.480 --> 00:18:52.030
Right now, Aoyama is a waste of space!
Let's put them away!

00:18:52.030 --> 00:18:55.050
Since Aoyama can't move, 
we need to cover for him!

00:18:55.050 --> 00:18:56.900
Yeah, we just have to do it!

00:18:57.210 --> 00:18:59.610
It's 2-2, and neither team is yielding!

00:18:59.610 --> 00:19:03.580
There isn't much time left,
so the next goal will decide the game.

00:18:59.610 --> 00:19:03.580
<b>Takada</b>

00:18:59.610 --> 00:19:03.580
<b>1st</b>

00:18:59.610 --> 00:19:03.580
<b>2nd</b>

00:18:59.610 --> 00:19:03.580
<b>ET</b>

00:18:59.610 --> 00:19:03.580
<b>Fujimi</b>

00:19:03.580 --> 00:19:04.530
There!

00:19:04.530 --> 00:19:05.550
No!

00:19:05.550 --> 00:19:07.540
Fujimi's defending for their lives,

00:19:07.740 --> 00:19:11.000
but with Aoyama in that state,
this will be tough.

00:19:15.160 --> 00:19:18.170
We've somehow kept it tied,
 but it's starting to look hopeless.

00:19:19.310 --> 00:19:21.380
Less than five minutes left!

00:19:25.060 --> 00:19:27.310
Takada Academy's attacks are relentless!

00:19:28.110 --> 00:19:30.270
I've got it!

00:19:35.320 --> 00:19:36.900
<i>I thought...</i>

00:19:36.900 --> 00:19:39.030
<i>you couldn't move.</i>

00:19:40.290 --> 00:19:43.570
Wow, he controlled that piledriver
on his chest!

00:19:43.570 --> 00:19:45.780
And now, he's counterattacking!

00:19:46.520 --> 00:19:48.520
<i>I'll make you go flying again!</i>

00:19:48.520 --> 00:19:49.500
Wha—

00:19:50.710 --> 00:19:54.670
This is a complete departure from his 
earlier finesse. He's going in hard!

00:19:54.670 --> 00:19:56.940
He came back out of his shell.

00:19:56.940 --> 00:19:57.630
Yeah.

00:19:58.290 --> 00:20:01.020
Aoyama hates losing more than dying.

00:20:01.020 --> 00:20:03.090
When he reaches the last five minutes...

00:20:03.090 --> 00:20:07.510
Stop, you little turd!

00:20:07.830 --> 00:20:12.060
the shackles of his germaphobia...

00:20:14.900 --> 00:20:16.550
can no longer keep him down!

00:20:24.280 --> 00:20:28.240
He scores! All by himself! 
A lightning counterattack!

00:20:29.230 --> 00:20:32.210
3-2! Fujimi High School pulls ahead!

00:20:33.080 --> 00:20:34.670
What is it with you?!

00:20:34.670 --> 00:20:37.630
I thought you hated getting dirty!

00:20:37.970 --> 00:20:41.280
I hate dirty things.

00:20:41.900 --> 00:20:43.080
Chief among them...

00:20:43.960 --> 00:20:45.940
Dirty cheats.

00:20:48.710 --> 00:20:52.960
So I'm going to crush you 
with everything I've got.

00:20:56.190 --> 00:20:57.440
Unacceptable.

00:20:57.960 --> 00:21:03.360
Aoyama's a monster in the youth division
who's never lost, not even once.

00:21:09.740 --> 00:21:14.500
Time's up! In the end, Fujimi wins 5-2!

00:21:11.690 --> 00:21:14.500
We did it, we did it!

00:21:17.460 --> 00:21:19.320
Yeah!

00:21:21.380 --> 00:21:22.840
Aoyama!

00:21:25.010 --> 00:21:27.310
Learn your lesson already, guys.

00:21:31.640 --> 00:21:33.530
What <i>is</i> this?

00:21:34.230 --> 00:21:36.490
Why is the clubhouse so clean?

00:21:36.490 --> 00:21:39.690
So Aoyama wasn't locked in here,
but stayed back to clean?!

00:21:40.000 --> 00:21:43.650
Aoyama-kun!

00:21:48.810 --> 00:21:50.580
Thank you! Thank you!

00:21:50.580 --> 00:21:54.140
Aoyama-kun! You're so cool!

00:21:54.140 --> 00:21:56.150
Kana!

00:23:31.910 --> 00:23:34.320
You're a germaphobe,
but you're on a sports team.

00:23:34.320 --> 00:23:37.060
That's hard to fathom, Aoyama.

00:23:37.060 --> 00:23:41.500
<b>Next time</b>

00:23:37.060 --> 00:23:41.500
<b>Narita-kun Keeps It a Secret</b>
